erience.","source_heading":"PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS","source_subheading":null},{"item_type":"experience","requirement_level":"preferred","item_text":"Specimen processing experience.","source_heading":"PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS","source_subheading":null},{"item_type":"experience","requirement_level":"preferred","item_text":"Recent CPT experience.","source_heading":"PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS","source_subheading":null},{"item_type":"job_duty","requirement_level":null,"item_text":"The Certified Phlebotomy Technician (CPT) performs timely and accurate blood draws for inpatients, emergency department patients, and outpatients of all ages. They are responsible for specimen processing, accessioning, phlebotomy, heel and finger sticks, customer service, clerical duties, problem resolution, record keeping, supply inventory and maintenance, and maintaining a clean and safe work environment. Additional responsibilities include effective communication with laboratory customers, operation of instruments, and preventive maintenance appropriate to the assigned section/department. Performs all duties in a manner consistent with current laboratory safety standards. Maintains a current Phlebotomy Certification issued by the State of California Laboratory Field Services.","source_heading":"DESCRIPTION","source_subheading":null},{"item_type":"qualification","requirement_level":"required","item_text":"Demonstrated competency in specimen collection, specimen preparation, storage, and disposal procedures.","source_heading":"MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS","source_subheading":null},{"item_type":"skill","requirement_level":"required","item_text":"Demonstrated knowledge of medical and scientific terminology.","source_heading":"MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS","source_subheading":null},{"item_type":"skill","requirement_level":"required","item_text":"Knowledge of laboratory regulations, safety standards, and ethical requirements.","source_heading":"MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS","source_subheading":null},{"item_type":"